Testing Plan:
    Our program functions as a simple shell environment, that is capable of running in batch and interactive mode 
        We tested various functions in the three modes, (no argument batch mode, no argument interactive, batch mode argument)
            functioned as expected 
        Our shell is successfully capable of handling file redirection using the following tokens
            > < | 
        We tested various commands including the following
            cd pwd which exit, and common Unix commands
            compiles/runs executable files 
            successfully exits and returns with the error signal/code upon an error or malformed input 
    Compiled with -fsanitaize=address to ensure no memory leaks/improper malloc usage

to run our shell environment: 
    make
    ./mysh.o with no args or one arg 
        use exit to leave interactive mode 

